# vllm-toolchest environment configuration
#
# You do not normally need this file. `./setup.sh install` detects your GPUs
# and container runtime, asks which image variant, which GPUs and which ports
# to use, and writes .env for you. It also preserves anything it does not own,
# so hand-edited values survive a later install or rebuild.
#
# This file documents what can go in .env if you would rather set it yourself:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Keys setup.sh manages: VLLMCTL_PORT, VLLMCTL_INFERENCE_PORT, VLLMCTL_VARIANT,
# VLLMCTL_MODELS_DIR, HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES, GPU_ARCH, HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION,
# HOST_VIDEO_GID, HOST_RENDER_GID.

# ─── Port configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────
VLLMCTL_PORT=3000
VLLMCTL_INFERENCE_PORT=8000

# ─── Image variant ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by `./setup.sh install` and reused by every later command.
#   generic   ROCm + vLLM built from source, tracking vLLM main. Portable.
#   radiance  This UI layered on the third-party vllm-radiance image, tuned
#             for RDNA4 / gfx1201. Requires an R9700 / RX 9070-class card.
#             https://codeberg.org/StillDeadcode/vllm-radiance
#VLLMCTL_VARIANT=generic

# ─── GPU selection ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which GPUs to hand to vLLM, by HIP index (setup.sh asks, and lists them).
# Omit the line to use every GPU -- an EMPTY value means "no GPUs" to HIP,
# not "all of them". Never use CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES on ROCm.
#HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1

# ─── Shared memory ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vLLM's multiprocess executor puts its inter-process message queue in
# /dev/shm. The container default is 64 MB, which is not enough to start an
# engine at any tensor-parallel size > 1:
#   RuntimeError: Insufficient space in /dev/shm: 160 MiB required, 62 MiB free
# 8 GB is generous and costs nothing until used (tmpfs allocates on write).
#
# Applies to the compose path only. The auto-start (Quadlet) unit runs with
# --ipc=host, which hands the container the host's /dev/shm -- there is nothing
# left to size, and podman refuses the two together.
#VLLMCTL_SHM_SIZE=8gb

# ─── Model storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bind-mount a host directory for model persistence across container rebuilds.
# Used with: docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.models.yml up
#VLLMCTL_MODELS_DIR=/home/user/llm-models

# ─── HuggingFace ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for gated models (Llama, Mistral, Gemma, etc.)
#HF_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── API Key ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Protect the /v1 proxy endpoint with a Bearer token
#VLLMCTL_API_KEY=

# ─── vLLM defaults ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These can also be set in the web UI (Settings page)
#VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTIL=0.90
#VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=0
#VLLM_TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=1
#VLLM_TOOL_USE_ENABLED=true

# ─── AMD ROCm settings ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auto-detected. Only override if needed.
#HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=12.0.1

# Host group IDs for GPU device access inside the container.
# Find with: getent group video | cut -d: -f3
#HOST_VIDEO_GID=
#HOST_RENDER_GID=

# ─── Build pinning ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AMD ROCm release from repo.radeon.com. 7.2.1 supports RDNA4 (gfx1201).
#ROCM_VERSION=7.2.1
#VLLM_VERSION=main

# Target GPU architecture(s). Semicolon-separated list for multi-arch builds.
# Defaults to gfx1201 (RDNA4: R9700, RX 9070/XT) + gfx1100 (RDNA3: 7900 XTX, W7900).
# Narrow to a single arch to shrink build time and wheel size.
#GPU_ARCH=gfx1201;gfx1100

# ─── Variant build inputs ───────────────────────────────────────────
# setup.sh writes these from the chosen variant's manifest
# (variants/<id>.conf) on every install, so editing them here does not stick.
# To change one for good, edit the manifest. To override a base image for a
# single build, set VLLMCTL_BASE_IMAGE in your shell instead:
#
#   VLLMCTL_BASE_IMAGE=docker.io/someone/their-build:1.2 ./setup.sh rebuild
#
# The base image and the vLLM pin move together: the FP8 tuner script is
# fetched from that tag and the build asserts the image's actual vLLM version
# matches. Keep the docker.io/ prefix -- podman fails on an unqualified name.
#
#VLLMCTL_VENDOR=amd
#VLLMCTL_BASE_IMAGE=docker.io/stilldeadcode/vllm-radiance:0.9.3
#VLLMCTL_DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.prebuilt
#VLLMCTL_VLLM_PIN=v0.27.1

# ─── Variant feature switches ───────────────────────────────────────
# GENERATED from variants/*.conf by `make env-example`. Edit the manifest,
# not this block; anything typed between the markers is overwritten.
#
# LEAVE THESE COMMENTED unless you are changing one. An empty value is not
# "unset" -- these images read it as "off", which disables the very feature
# the variant exists for. All of them can also be set from the Settings page,
# and a value set there wins over one set here.
#
# >>> BEGIN GENERATED KNOBS

# ── Radiance (RDNA4 / gfx1201) — VLLMCTL_VARIANT=radiance ──
# https://codeberg.org/StillDeadcode/vllm-radiance
#
# R4D kernel library. Master switch for the hand-written gfx1201 kernel
# library (libr4d): paged attention, the gated-delta-net scan, vision
# attention, the P2P all-reduce and the skinny GEMM. Off reverts every
# one of them to the stock path.
#RADIANCE_USE_R4D=1
#
# P2P all-reduce. The TP=2 peer-to-peer one-shot all-reduce.
# Bit-identical to RCCL either way; off keeps RCCL.
#RADIANCE_USE_R4D_AR=1
#
# All-reduce quantization. Compresses large (prefill) all-reduce
# payloads. This one is NOT bit-identical to RCCL — turn it off if you
# need the exact bf16 all-reduce.
#RADIANCE_USE_R4D_AR_QUANT=1
#
# Preshuffled FP8 GEMM. Preshuffled weight layout for the block-FP8
# GEMM.
#RADIANCE_PRESHUFFLE=1
#
# Fused RMSNorm + quant. Fused RMSNorm + group-FP8-quant path.
#RADIANCE_FUSE_RMS_QUANT=1
#
# Skinny bf16 GEMM. Routes small-M bf16 projections to the R4D split-K
# kernel. "all" adds shapes that differ from rocBLAS at a bf16 ULP —
# notably the gated-delta-net in_proj_ba.
#RADIANCE_SKINNY_GEMM=1
#
# Speculative drafting.
# Only applies to models started with a speculative config. Lossless
# either way: the target model verifies every drafted token with its
# own weights.
#
# Dynamic draft depth. Per-request MTP draft depth chosen by a
# confidence gate, plus verbatim n-gram tails. Off is byte-identical
# stock MTP.
#RADIANCE_DYNAMIC_DRAFT=1
#
# Fast draft head. The 2-bit draft head with exact rerank, plus 4-bit
# dflash drafter weights. Keep in sync with the confidence gate below:
# radiance tunes 0.28 for the 2-bit head and 0.35 for the stock bf16
# one.
#RADIANCE_FAST_DRAFT=1
#
# Draft confidence (tau). Confidence gate for the draft depth. 0.28 is
# tuned for the 2-bit head, 0.35 for the stock bf16 one — leaving them
# crossed drafts deeper than the head pays for. Blank uses the image
# default.
#RADIANCE_DRAFT_TAU=
#
# Draft schedule. Caps serial MTP forwards by batch size, as
# batch:depth pairs. Blank uses the image default.
#RADIANCE_DRAFT_SCHEDULE=1:8,2:7,4:6,8:5,16:4
#
# Startup bandwidth sweep. Topology, P2P access matrix, NUMA distances
# and peak copy bandwidth per agent pair at startup. Backgrounded and
# about a second, so it never delays the serve.
#RADIANCE_RUN_BWTEST=1
#
# NUMA binding. Pin the vLLM fleet to the GPU-local NUMA node(s). No-op
# on single-node hosts. "auto" detects; explicit nodes also work (e.g.
# 0 or 0,1). Needs the SYS_NICE capability.
#RADIANCE_NUMA_BIND=
# <<< END GENERATED KNOBS
